# Ruleset — D&D 5e

Default ruleset for v1. Edition choice (2014 vs 2024) is set at session start in `character-creator-core.mdc`.

## Step order by edition

| Step | `currentStep` (2014) | `currentStep` (2024) |
|------|----------------------|----------------------|
| 1 | `choose_race` | `choose_class` |
| 2 | `choose_class` | `choose_origin` |
| 3 | `ability_scores` | `ability_scores` |
| 4 | `background_personality` | `choose_alignment` |
| 5 | `equipment` | `choose_species` |
| 6 | `review` | `equipment` |
| 7 | — | `personality_review` |

Follow the column matching the session edition. Do not reorder without player consent.

## Per-step guidance

For each step: state what must be decided, what is deferred, search + cite rule text from `character-creator-research.mdc`, ask one cluster at a time, always offer **Other / custom (describe)**.

### 2014 steps

Full 2014 guidance lives in dedicated rules (do not skip):

| Topic | Rule file |
|-------|-----------|
| Step order, PHB catalogs, mechanics | `ruleset-dnd5e-2014-core.mdc` |
| Official expansions, source selection, UA | `ruleset-dnd5e-2014-expansions.mdc` |

2014 differs from 2024: race-first creation, racial ASI, backgrounds without ASI/feats, subclass timing varies by class, Inspiration (not Heroic).

### 2024 steps

Full 2024 guidance lives in dedicated rules (do not skip):

| Topic | Rule file |
|-------|-----------|
| Step order, PHB catalogs, mechanics | `ruleset-dnd5e-2024-core.mdc` |
| Official expansions, source selection, replacement rules | `ruleset-dnd5e-2024-expansions.mdc` |

2024 differs from 2014: class-first creation, backgrounds grant ASI + Origin feat, species have no ASI, all subclasses at level 3, Weapon Mastery for martials.

## Derived stats (after prerequisites confirmed)

Compute only from confirmed choices; cite formulas in Sources:

- Proficiency bonus, HP (hit die + CON mod), AC, speed, initiative
- Saving throws and skills (with proficiency flags)
- Attack bonuses, spell save DC, spell attack bonus
- Spell slots / prepared spells / known spells as applicable

Ask the player to confirm derived block before marking `complete`.

## JSON fields

Use the template in `characters/_templates/character.template.json`. Key fields:

- `ruleset`: `"dnd5e"`
- `edition`: `"2014"` | `"2024"`
- `currentStep`: step id from table above
- `identity`, `abilityScores`, `proficiencies`, `equipment`, `personality`, `features`, `spells`, `derived`, `sources`

Keep `character.md` and `character.json` in sync after each step.
